  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4a076659-85a1-54f9-867e-aa8c3da0e47a" activityNameId="96525bdb-f647-5596-818c-05ff4df1ea0a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, peat, at power plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, peat, at power plant
Due to lack of specific information, the emission data were assumed to be same as for German average lignite plants, whose fuel has a similar heating value. The following information refers to this German lignite plant. The module describes the electricity production of an average plant for the country. The plant is used for middle load with 6000 hours of operation at full capacity per year. The plant is assumed to operate 200000 hours during its lifetime. For the assessment of main characteristics (LHV, sulphur and ash content of coal, efficiency of the plant) and criteria emissions (SOx, NOx, particles, and CO2) a bottom-up approach has been used. It consists on the collection of information about single plants. Base data on all major UCTE power plants in 1993 have been integrated, to the extent possible, with updated information for year 2000. The size distribution of particles has been derived from German data. Halogene emissions have been estimated on the basis of the content of the species in the country-specific coal input mix, assuming average retention rates. For CO and VOC-emissions average values for UCTE are included. Two average values for N2O emissions from UCTE plants are considered for the two cases with or without DeNOx;
UUID: 183c1890-9dc2-3141-a8de-6aafca48711d
Electricity output at busbar. The module uses the average net efficiency of peat power plants in NORDEL countries.
Location: Country-specific data.
Technology: Average installed technology.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature and statistics 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_183c1890-9dc2-3141-a8de-6aafca48711d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
